//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Implement k stacks in an array
You are given two integers n and k. Implement a class kStacks that uses a single array of size n to simulate k independent stacks.

Required Operations:
1. push(x, i) - Push element x into the i-th stack
2. pop(i) - Pop top element from i-th stack, return -1 if empty

Input Format:
- n: size of array
- k: number of stacks
- q: number of queries
- queries[][]: array of queries
  - [1, x, i] means push(x, i)
  - [2, i] means pop(i)

Constraints:
- 1 <= q <= 10^5
- 1 <= k <= n <= 10^5
- Stack values: 0 to 10^9

Your Approach: Linked List within Array
- Use arr[] for values, top[] for stack tops, next[] for links
- Maintain free list for dynamic slot allocation
- All operations O(1) time, O(n + k) space

Time: O(1) per operation | Space: O(n + k)
